        "id": "ch17_2-3",
        "text": "\u00bb  Rename: Change the system name of the printer.\n\u00bb\n\u00bb  Delete: Deletes the selected printer.\n\u00bb\n\u00bb  Enabled: Allow print jobs to be serviced by the printer when checked.\nFIGURE 17-8:\nThe Ubuntu\nPrinter\n-Configuration\nwindow.\nCHAPTER 17 Basic System Administration 333\n\u00bb\n\u00bb  Shared: When checked, this feature advertises the printer on the network for\nother Linux workstations using CUPS to connect to.\n\u00bb\n\u00bb  Set as Default: Use this printer by default when printing from an application.\n\u00bb\n\u00bb  View Print Queue: List the print jobs waiting to be printed by the printer.\nThe following sections describe how to use the Printer Configuration window to\nset the CUPS and printer properties for your system.\nEsta secci\u00f3n contiene las siguientes subsecciones\n\u2022 Printer server settings\n\u2022 Adding a new printer\n\u2022 Modifying printer properties\nSi deseas explorar cualquiera de estas subsecciones, puedes pregunt\u00e1rmelo directamente.",
